# LDAPBrowser - A CLI LDAP browser bash application.

A lightweight bash application designed to view/browse various LDAP directories on a Linux/Unix system.

## Key Features

- **Real-time LDAP Browsing**: Automatic message loading with background monitoring (2-second intervals)
- **Various LDAP Directories Supported**:
		AD, IPA, OpenLDAP, JumpCloud, Foxpass
- **Authentication**: Username+Password, Username+Password and OTP
- **Security**: LDAP with StartTLS
- **Colorful Interface**: Supported a few color schemes to choose from
- **Neat Features Inside**: Preview window to view the selected DN entry,
							fast copy all the selected DN's attributes into the clipboard,
							easy browsing like a filesystem,
							immediate app exit if needed at any browsing stage,
							various logging levels for the app
							

## Technical Specifications

- **Platform**: Linux/Unix systems
- **Dependencies**: bash, 
- **Architecture**: Single script with commands implemented as modules with separate functions,
					dependencies and connectivity checks,
					various logging levels available,
					example various configurations available.

## Use Cases

Perfect for one IT person or IT teams that need secure, terminal-based LDAP read-only access on Linux/Unix systems.
Ideal for system administrators, devops or any IT group requiring view access on Linux/Unix systems to local and cloud LDAP directories.

## Security Model

Uses the standard username+password into an LDAP directory via the LDAP with StartTLS protocols.
